{"type":"message","id":"3daffef4","parentId":"d09768cd","timestamp":"2026-05-20T10:02:24.216Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - GET /send returns a simple string \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\". So the send endpoint exists, but POST is failing with error 1101. This could mean:\n1. POST /send expects a different payload structure\n2. The worker has a bug when processing POST\n3. There might be rate limiting\n\nLet me try different payload formats.\n\nActually, looking at this, maybe the 1101 is not a Cloudflare error code but a custom error from the platform. Let me try to check if the history endpoint works without the API key, or with a different format.\n\nThe fact that `POST /send` fails consistently but `GET /send` works suggests the POST handler might have an issue.\n\n\nLet me test a different approach and see if the headers or query parameters make a difference.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4325b4e7-80c2-4713-bbb6-afda6769e211","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -v -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"content\":\"[Heartbeat] Test message\"}' 2>&1 | tail -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":582,"output":272,"cacheRead":18208,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19062,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779271331664,"responseId":"chatcmpl-73b0e592-cfe7-4363-8d85-d4ef07f5c2d7"}}
